<title>USA: Micro Component gets $1.2 mln order.</title>
<headline>Micro Component gets $1.2 mln order.</headline>
<dateline>ST. PAUL, Minn. 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Micro Component Technology Inc said Tuesday it had received an order for its 5100 high speed SOIC handlers valued at about $1.2 million.</p>
<p>The units are expected to be manufactured and shipped during calendar 1997.</p>
<p>The 5100 is a high speed gravity feed handler focused on the SOIC market (0.110 inches to 0.300 inches) with a total throughput of 14,400 devices per hour.</p>
<p>MCT makes automated test handling equipment for the semiconductor industry.</p>
<p>((-- Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
